{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion","id":993662,"title":"Dreamwalking devotion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-26T13:16:59-07:00","id":993662,"title":"Dreamwalking devotion","content":"Has anyone come up with an Auspex Devotion that would allow a vampire to enter and manipulate dreams? It seems like it would be really useful for a Vampire/Changeling or Vampire/Beast crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:32:36-07:00","id":993668,"title":"","content":"I'd say base Auspex 5 as a passive observer and add a little Majesty/Nightmare/Obfuscate to actually influence things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:34:28-07:00","id":993669,"title":"","content":"Auspex + Nightmare?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:52:38-07:00","id":993681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=993669#post993669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex + Nightmare?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Auspex 5 since it already gives you an ephemeral projection, and Nightmare (probably 3 since that allows you to partly shape the victim's mind) since the two official devotions in 2E that affects dreams includes Nightmare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:45:32-07:00","id":993774,"title":"","content":"There was a bloodline, the Alucinor, who were involved with dreams and manipulating them. Their signature disciplines were Auspex and Obfuscate, with Celerity as a physical. They had a discipline, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Insomnium\" target=\"_blank\">Insomnium</a> that let them do most of it. You might look to them for a foundation for something more fitting in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T03:43:38-07:00","id":993964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=993774#post993774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a bloodline, the Alucinor, who were involved with dreams and manipulating them. Their signature disciplines were Auspex and Obfuscate, with Celerity as a physical. They had a discipline, <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Insomnium\" target=\"_blank\">Insomnium</a> that let them do most of it. You might look to them for a foundation for something more fitting in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I rebuilt them with Nightmare as a fourth discipline and the powers being Devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T05:38:44-07:00","id":993999,"title":"","content":"Wet Dream devotion already lets you shape a dream. Telepathy traditionally can watch dreams. Auspex 1/majesty 1 devotion from 1e while biting someone let you in the dream as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T07:24:14-07:00","id":994018,"title":"","content":"Like MCN said. There is already a devotion that lets you into a dream and has perimeters on how far the manipulation can go. I would think if you wanted more control over what they dream make a devotion that builds upon the first. maybe Majesty 2 nightmare 2 and Wet dream to bolster it... or another route is that devotions often use vigor to make them stronger. So you could have a devotion with the prerequisite Wet dream and Vigor 2 or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:00:31-07:00","id":994136,"title":"","content":"Wait are we talking about<b></b>: Entering , Shaping , or Viewing dreaming?<br /> <br /> Also. There's some thats been done here about updating Insomnium to 2ed standards. Might be worth a read ::<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/111826-alucinor-in-blood-smoke\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...in-blood-smoke</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T23:12:11-07:00","id":994424,"title":"","content":"I'll take a look. And MCN, I wasn't talking about just influencing or viewing, but actually entering dreams the way Changelings and Beasts can. Maybe entering the capital d Dream as well. <br /> <br /> The problem with Auspex 5 is it's kind of on the high side, but other than that it seems easy enough. And I'm generally sticking to B+S philosophy of using Devotions instead of new Disciplines, especially since dream powers are the sort of thing that would be very easy to handle as adjustments of the core Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Here's how I'd handle it: Seeing into dreams is already handled by Auspex, so I'd make the following a devotion set, probably learnable by any vampire (since if I actually did this in a chronicle, I wouldn't want to force any of the players into playing the only bloodline with dream powers).<br /> <br /> Auspex+Majesty: Enter dreams. <br /> <br /> Auspex+Nightmare: Cause Tilts/Conditions in sleeping people by attacking their dreams. More effective if the vampire is actually inside the dream. Can also be used to drive out other entities, since the illusions created by Nightmare are &quot;real&quot; within the dreamworld. <br /> <br /> Auspex+Obfuscate: Shape dreams in other ways. Hiding or changing information, creating barriers, and so on. Similarly to Nightmare, Obfuscate illusions are more &quot;real&quot; when summoned inside dreams. <br /> <br /> Auspex 5: Your astral projection can enter dreams as well. <br /> <br /> I'm probably going to wait for Changeling 2e and the Beast Player's Guide, since both are probably going to have info on doing stuff in dreams, but that's a preliminary outline. I definitely want to get in that illusionary Disciplines allow for limited reality warping when used in dreams. So a monster summoned with Nightmare is as &quot;solid&quot; as anything else in a dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-28-2016, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T06:22:15-07:00","id":994532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=994424#post994424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take a look. And MCN, I wasn't talking about just influencing or viewing, but actually entering dreams the way Changelings and Beasts can. Maybe entering the capital d Dream as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> The closest thing to a capital D-dream is the so-called Primordial Dream, which actually has nothing to do with real dreams. Its part of the Astral and its three levels, a dark reflection of the collective unconciousness of humanity and their relationship to the natural world. But to call it a Dream is misleading. Actual dreams exist outside of the Astral, as per David Brookshaw. At best, dreams touch on the Astral and Hedge and serve as a bridge before fading away into their own thing. And, curiously enough, Beasts actually have very little to do with regular dreams. The Begotten can use a sleeper as a gateway to the Astral, and upset a person's dreams, but they don't actually stay in the dreams. You just pass through it momentarily before being shunted entirely in the Astral. Horrors can act independantly and slip into a dream to feed on it, but that's not something the PC actually does; its outside of their control. At best, someone can argue that you -might- be able to find some kind of pathway from someone's Onerios into their dreams, but I've never seen any rules or guidelines for it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Changelings physically -enter- the dream to the point their body disappears, and experience dreams as an extension of Hedge-walking. That is nothing like a Beast and their pseudo-relationship to actual dreams. Plus, I somehow doubt that you're talking about having a vampire make body vanish from reality and turn into dream-material. So, when you say &quot;like Beasts and Changelings,&quot; that is a bit misleading, since that's rather something I don't think would make sense.<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the record, entering the Astral through use of Auspex 4 is cannon, as per the Astral Realms book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-28-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:11:13-07:00","id":994553,"title":"","content":"Auspex 4 in 1E (that the Astral Realms is written for) and 2E are extremely similar, but functions somewhat different. Telepathy works by projecting your consciousness into your subject. From there it's just a matter of going from the consciousness and memories to dreams. Lay Open the Mind on the other hand is &quot;just&quot; connecting two minds. To be able to &quot;physically&quot; visit the subject's dreams you'd have to create a projection of yourself inside the subject's mind or dreams. That's my rationale as for why Auspex 5 would be required to visit a subject's dreams, but since Auspex in 1E already could do that I'd keep the devotion to just Auspex 5 and not include Nightmare, as I previously suggested.<br /> <br /> Other than that I second that some clarification is needed about the Dream with a capital D. I've written with the assumption it's only about the personal dream plane. The Oneiros is more difficult, and Temenos likely impossible for a vampire to enter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-28-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:45:00-07:00","id":994799,"title":"","content":"I was talking about the Primordial Dream as the &quot;capital d&quot; dream. And I'm not talking about physical travel as much as creating a projection inside the dreamer's mind. I'm not sure this would require full Astral projection when you already have mind control and illusions- the way I see it is that the vampire is essentially forcing the dreamer's mind to create an image of the vampire inside itself, and I like that because it plays off the exploitative and parasitic nature of vampires. <br /> <br /> And I wasn't talking about the Astral, yeah. I'm fine with vampires having nothing to do with the Temenos. <br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure the Beast PG is going to have some more dream stuff, at least. I'm aware that Beasts and Changelings interact with dreams differently, but they're thematically close enough that you could fudge some things if you really wanted to work it, and I kinda feel like that's what Beast and crossovers in general are about. If you want to do Inception with vampires, changelings, and beasts, this is so you could give it a try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:43:24-07:00","id":994905,"title":"","content":"I did a writeup of the Alucinor, if it interests you at all: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rPxt855Ms1DGTmF8xl4IP1cNGfKDTRazIQNyLifoLkE/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...NyLifoLkE/edit</a><br /> Basically uses a few devotions, but I also did a small writeup of Insomnium as Blood Sorcery which is linked in there too as an option. Both versions have a Dream Form ruleset for Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:18:54-07:00","id":995007,"title":"","content":"Very useful, I'll take a look at it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:26:07-07:00","id":995252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=994799#post994799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about the Primordial Dream as the &quot;capital d&quot; dream. .... And I wasn't talking about the Astral, yeah. I'm fine with vampires having nothing to do with the Temenos.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummmm? The Primordial Dream is part of the Astral. Its part of the Temenos. So, the moment you mention the Primordial or Beasts, you talk about the Astral. There are no rules, guidelines or suggestions for how a Beast will interact with dreams. Just some suggestions for the Horror, and only in extremely vague terms. <br /> <br /> It sounds like you have a bit of the cosmology mixed up here, Gecko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:54:50-07:00","id":995329,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the Primordial Dream and the Temenos were both parts of the Astral, and the Temenos was the part that only humans and mages can access. <br /> <br /> I could have phrased it better, but when I said &quot;I wasn't talking about the astral&quot;, I was saying that the primary purpose of the thread was to figure out a way for vampires to enter individual dreams, which, as you've said, aren't part of the Astral. <br /> <br /> And the reason I've been mentioning the player's guide is because I know the corebook doesn't have many guidelines, and it's something I'd imagine will be covered there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:29:43-07:00","id":996084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=995329#post995329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the Primordial Dream and the Temenos were both parts of the Astral, and the Temenos was the part that only humans and mages can access.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify it: They are both part of the Astral, by virtue of the Primordial Dream being part of the Temenos. It is the deepest darkest part of the Temenos, home to humanities collective fears and nightmares. Beasts can access the rest of Temenos (outside their Lair) with a Primordial Pathway. It is also mentioned that Mages have a hard time accesing the lowest part of the Temenos on their own, they can't go into Lairs the same way they travel the rest of the Astral. Sleepers cannot access the Temenos on their own, but they do affect it. They can't access their own Onieros either, even with it being a part of them. They can 'access' their own dreams obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:49:38-07:00","id":996095,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think I've got it. I think the mention of the Astral confused people, since I was mostly just thinking of how make a universally learnable changeling-style dream travel devotion beyond just the Alucinor, and I threw in a mention of the Primordial Dream as another possible application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:59:34-07:00","id":996101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/993662-dreamwalking-devotion?p=996095#post996095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think I've got it. I think the mention of the Astral confused people, since I was mostly just thinking of how make a universally learnable changeling-style dream travel devotion beyond just the Alucinor, and I threw in a mention of the Primordial Dream as another possible application.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought so, but didn't want to leave the false impression there in case anyone new came into the thread and it confused them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}